{
  "requirement": "{impl}`requirements.configuration.feature_sections`\n`--config <name>` MUST select a configuration for that invocation. Otherwise,\nauthoring MUST use the user's selection for the canonical project root, then the\nworkspace default, then the user's default. Named workspace configurations MUST\noverride same-named user configurations as complete records. Backend, model,\nconnection settings, and options MUST come from the selected record as a unit;\nfields MUST NOT be merged between records. Workspace-only authoring MUST work\nwithout a user configuration file. Missing configuration or an unknown selection\nMUST identify the relevant configuration file and point to documented examples.\n\nAn explicit Bedrock AWS profile or region MUST override the corresponding SDK\ndefault; omitted values MUST use standard AWS SDK resolution. Ollama MUST use\nits configured endpoint or `http://localhost:11434`. If `api_key_env` is set, its\nnamed variable MUST supply the credential; a missing or empty value MUST produce\nan error before a model request. OpenAI MUST use its configured endpoint or\n`https://api.openai.com/v1`, and MUST resolve `OPENAI_API_KEY` when neither\n`api_key` nor `api_key_env` is supplied.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judge the tests adequate for `requirements.authoring.configuration_precedence`. I did not read implementation source. Each obligation maps to tests as follows.\n\n**Selection order**\n- `tests/configuration.rs#fn[workspace_defaults_and_configs_combine_with_existing_user_selections]` and `#fn[explicit_project_and_default_selections_choose_whole_configs]` cover the order.\n- An explicit name beats the project selection, which beats the workspace default, which beats the user default.\n- A workspace default can name a user config.\n- With no workspace default, resolution falls back to the user default.\n- The project root is matched in canonical form: the test resolves with `root.join(\".\")` and gets the entry stored under the canonical root.\n\n**`--config` selection**\n- The explicit-name cases above cover resolution.\n- The CLI passes `--config` in `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[an_explicit_configuration_selects_the_nondefault_workspace_profile]`.\n- The same test file includes a run with `--config missing`, in `#fn[usage_record_of_an_early_failure_identifies_its_subject_kind]`.\n\n**Whole-record override, no field merging**\n- In `#fn[workspace_defaults_and_configs_combine_with_existing_user_selections]`, a workspace `shared` replaces the user `shared`.\n  - Its backend is Ollama.\n  - Its options are `{temperature: 0.8}`, with no `top_p` carried over.\n  - `concurrency` is `None` and the endpoint is `None`.\n- `#fn[workspace_configurations_accept_validate_and_override_concurrency]` repeats the check for all three backends, with and without a workspace `concurrency`.\n\n**Workspace-only without a user file**\n- `tests/configuration.rs` resolves with a `None` user config.\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[authoring_uses_nearest_workspace_configuration_without_a_user_file]` runs the CLI end to end with the user file deleted. It sends a request with the workspace model and key, and it creates no user file.\n\n**Missing or unknown configuration errors**\n- `tests/configuration.rs#fn[unknown_selections_name_the_file_that_made_them]` covers the cases below. Each asserts that the file path appears in the error and that the error contains the `editing-the-file` documentation anchor.\n  - A dangling user default.\n  - A dangling project selection.\n  - A dangling workspace default.\n  - An unknown `--config` name.\n  - The no-workspace case.\n- `#fn[explicit_project_and_default_selections_choose_whole_configs]` covers the missing-configuration case.\n- `#fn[configurations_without_any_selection_report_how_to_choose_one]` covers the case where configs exist but none is selected.\n\n**Bedrock**\n- `providers.rs#mod[tests]/fn[omitted_bedrock_profile_and_region_use_standard_sdk_resolution]` asserts three things.\n  - Omitted values resolve exactly as the plain SDK does.\n  - An explicit profile is used.\n  - An explicit region overrides the profile's region.\n- `providers.rs#mod[tests]/fn[explicit_bedrock_credentials_reach_the_sdk_without_the_default_chain]` runs with `AWS_PROFILE` and the env credentials set. The explicit region `us-west-2` still wins over the profile's `us-east-1`.\n- `authoring_cli.rs#fn[bedrock_cli_uses_selected_profile_region_and_converse_tools]` checks the signed profile key and the `us-west-2` region in the request headers.\n- `authoring_cli.rs#fn[all_adapters_preserve_prompt_tools_and_evidence_with_default_connections]` checks the default chain. With no profile or region configured, the request uses the env key and the `ap-south-1` region.\n\n**Ollama and OpenAI**\n- The default Ollama endpoint is asserted through `endpoint()` in `#fn[backend_configuration_round_trips_without_materializing_defaults]`.\n- The default OpenAI endpoint is asserted through `endpoint()` in `#fn[openai_configuration_preserves_model_and_resolves_credentials]`.\n- Configured endpoints are exercised by the CLI tests against local servers.\n- The CLI test with no Ollama auth sends no authorization header.\n- `OPENAI_API_KEY` is resolved when no key is configured. This is checked through the `api_key_from` closure, which asserts the variable name, and through a CLI run that sets the env var.\n\n**`api_key_env`**\n- The named variable supplies the credential in the Ollama and OpenAI unit tests and in the CLI tests.\n- `authoring_cli.rs#fn[missing_or_empty_api_key_env_fails_before_any_model_request]` covers a missing and an empty value for both Ollama and OpenAI. It asserts a non-zero exit, that stderr names the variable, that the listener never accepts a connection, and that the evidence file is unchanged.\n\nI found no unmarked relevant tests and no uncovered clause. Passing an explicit profile to the SDK loader is a direct pass-through, so the absence of a test for an explicit profile overriding a set `AWS_PROFILE` is not a gap.",
  "references": "170e622ae6b9832cff78c46785518be4aebdf1977a2808d26f8516b315dc0a07",
